cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Terrestrial Conservation Gap: Workflow and geospatial outcome for the Danish contribution to the 30% Target"
version: 1.0.0
type: dataset
license: MIT

message: "If you use this repository, please cite it using the metadata in this CITATION.cff file."

abstract: >
  Workflow, geospatial outputs, and R scripts used to reproduce the terrestrial analyses
  and geospatial outcome for Denmark’s contribution to the 30% land target, including
  Fig. 1 and Table S2 in the manuscript 'Identifying Conservation Gaps: A Framework for
  Evaluating National Contributions to the 30x30 Target'.

keywords:
  - protected areas effectiveness
  - 30 by 30 target
  - 30x30
  - EU Biodiversity Strategy
  - Natura 2000
  - conservation effectiveness
  - Denmark
  - terrestrial protected areas
  - spatial analysis
  - reproducible research

